From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] journal: use variant dictionary for unique-value query

The datastore D-Bus method declares its optional query as a{sv}.  Passing an
a{ss} dictionary is rejected by dbus-python on current runtimes and causes the
datastore service to disconnect while Journal initializes.

--- a/src/jarabe/journal/model.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/journal/model.py
@@ -661,7 +661,7 @@
 def get_unique_values(key):
     """Returns a list with the different values a property has taken
     """
-    empty_dict = dbus.Dictionary({}, signature='ss')
+    empty_dict = dbus.Dictionary({}, signature='sv')
     return _call_datastore('get_uniquevaluesfor', key, empty_dict)
